                <pb facs="0264" n="144" xml:id="pg144"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Chargé
                    Coolidge.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis states that in the matter of coal for belligerent war vessels the
                    Government of the United States is well disposed toward the Chinese Government
                    in her efforts to preserve neutrality.)</p>
            </div>
